      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ given that $a=⟨-2,0,4⟩$ and $b\\times c=⟨7,-4,9⟩.$",
      "worked_solution": "Substituting given vectors into the formula for the scalar triple product, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨-2,0,4⟩\\cdot ⟨7,-4,9⟩ \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot 7+0\\cdot (-4)+4\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =22.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
