      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ given that $a=⟨2\\sqrt{2},\\,-1,\\,4⟩$ and $b\\times c=⟨-2\\sqrt{2},\\,3,\\,-5⟩.$\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Substituting given vectors into the formula for the scalar triple product, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨2\\sqrt{2},\\,-1,\\,4⟩\\cdot ⟨-2\\sqrt{2},\\,3,\\,-5⟩ \\\\  & =(2\\sqrt{2})(-2\\sqrt{2})+(-1)(3)+(4)(-5) \\\\  & =-8-3-20 \\\\  & =-31.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
