    "q-20050": {
      "dom_id": "step-q20050",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Let $a=⟨1,3,2⟩$, $b=⟨3,4,1⟩$ and $c=⟨2,0,1⟩.$ Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c).$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the scalar triple product $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(4\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 1)-3(3\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 1)+2(3\\cdot 0-2\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =4-3-16 \\\\  & =-15.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
