    "q-317319": {
      "dom_id": "step-q317319",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Let $a=⟨2,1,3⟩$, $b=⟨1,4,0⟩$ and $c=⟨6,-1,2⟩.$ Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using a determinant.\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the scalar triple product $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|\\,-\\,1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 2\\end{aligned}|\\,+\\,3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\,(4\\cdot 2-0\\cdot (-1))\\,-\\,1\\,(1\\cdot 2-0\\cdot 6)\\,+\\,3\\,(1\\cdot (-1)-4\\cdot 6) \\\\  & =2\\,(8)\\,-\\,1\\,(2)\\,+\\,3\\,(-25) \\\\  & =16-2-75 \\\\  & =-61.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "dom_id": "freeResponseTextbox-1",
          "tag": "mathquill",
          "choices": [],
