      "source_example_id": "e-4348",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Scalar Triple Product Using a Determinant",
      "kp_id": "e-4348"
    },
    "q-317344": {
      "dom_id": "step-q317344",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "Find $c\\cdot (a\\times b),$ if $b\\times c=⟨7,-2,3⟩$ and $a=⟨1,4,2⟩.$\n\n$c\\cdot (a\\times b)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "First, we compute the triple scalar product \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨1,4,2⟩\\cdot ⟨7,-2,3⟩ \\\\  & =1\\cdot 7+4\\cdot (-2)+2\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =7-8+6 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $a$ and $c$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot (b\\times a)=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand again we swap $a$ and $b$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot (a\\times b)=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "dom_id": "freeResponseTextbox-1",
