      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "Find $c\\cdot (b\\times a)$, if $b\\times c=⟨-2,5,4⟩$ and $a=⟨-1,3,2⟩.$\n\n$c\\cdot (b\\times a)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "First, we compute the triple scalar product \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨-1,3,2⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,5,4⟩ \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot (-2)+3\\cdot 5+2\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =2+15+8 \\\\  & =25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $a$ and $c$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot (b\\times a)=-25.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
