      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "Find $b\\cdot (a\\times c)$, if $5a\\cdot ((-4b)\\times (-3c))=-120.$\n\n$b\\cdot (a\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "First, we factor out the constants and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5a\\cdot ((-4b)\\times (-3c)) & =-120 \\\\ 5\\cdot (-4)\\cdot (-3)\\cdot [a\\cdot (b\\times c)] & =-120 \\\\ 60[a\\cdot (b\\times c)] & =-120 \\\\ a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $a$ and $b$ to get\n\n$$\nb\\cdot (a\\times c)=2.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
